## 8. Derivation & audit note

This blueprint was derived from a private, running instance of the method — a real human + AI partnership, operated daily, in which every mechanism described here is in active use and every failure mode described here was learned from a specific, recorded error in that instance.

The instance itself is never published. Its figures, people, records, and circumstances are private, and they stay private — not as a marketing posture, but because they are not the reader's to audit and not needed for the reader to run the method. What is published is the method: the shapes, the formats, the rules, and the reasoning, complete enough for anyone to build their own instance from a standing start.

That division is the audit offer. We do not ask you to trust the private instance's results — there are no results here to trust, and this document has been careful to claim none. We ask you to run the method on your own work, keep your own ledger, and grade the claims against your own receipts. If the falsifiers in this blueprint are wrong, your ledger is exactly the instrument that will prove it — which is, in the end, the whole point.

*— The Upper Hand Method, v0.1. Free to copy, free to fork, free to improve. The blueprints are the method as practiced; when the practice improves, the blueprints are revised — and the revisions are dated, because that, too, is the method.*
